<div id="export-panel" style="display: none;">
  <div class="oscar-export">
    <div id="export-pages" class="oscar-export-warning" style="display: none;">
      <strong>Only the first page is published.</strong>
      This project has <span id="export-page-count"></span> pages, and a
      published interface is a single page.
    </div>

    <!-- The project on the canvas: who can open it, the one code for the
         address that goes with that, and one button that says what it does.
         What used to be explained in paragraphs above the button is behind
         the question mark; the misunderstanding behind every "my page does
         nothing" report (OSCAR has to keep running) is its first sentence. -->
    <div id="publish-card" class="oscar-publish-card">
      <div class="oscar-publish-card-head">
        <span id="publish-title" class="oscar-publish-title"></span>
        <span id="publish-card-access" class="oscar-publish-card-access"></span>
        <button
          id="publish-help"
          class="oscar-publish-help"
          type="button"
          aria-label="How publishing works"
          data-tooltip-pos="bottom"
          data-tooltip="OSCAR has to keep running: a browser cannot send OSC, DMX or MIDI on its own, so the page hands everything to OSCAR. Publishing makes a page of its own, separate from the editor, at an address phones and tablets open. It stays as it is while you carry on editing, until you publish the changes."
        >?</button>
      </div>
      <div id="publish-card-where"></div>
      <div class="oscar-publish-card-foot">
        <span id="publish-state" class="oscar-publish-state"></span>
        <button id="publish-button" class="o-btn o-btn-primary oscar-export-go" type="button">Publish</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="export-error" class="oscar-export-error" style="display: none;"></div>
    <div id="export-note" class="oscar-export-note" style="display: none;"></div>

    <!-- What an extension adds under the card. What else OSCAR is running is
         not here: that is the server's business, and has a window of its own. -->
    <div class="oscar-publish-columns">
      <!-- Where an extension adds to the dialog. Empty in OSCAR itself. -->
      <div id="publish-extras" class="oscar-publish-extras"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- Opened from a published interface's Download button, in place of the
         dialog: a file cannot ask where OSCAR is, so it is told here. -->
    <div id="download-panel" style="display: none;">
      <div class="oscar-export">
        <p class="oscar-export-lead">
          The same page as an <code>.html</code> file, to host on a web server
          or open on another computer. It does not work opened from a phone's
          or tablet's own storage; the published address is for those.
        </p>
        <div class="oscar-export-row">
          <div class="oscar-export-field">
            <label for="download-host">OSCAR is reachable at</label>
            <input id="download-host" class="o-input" type="text" spellcheck="false" />
          </div>
          <div class="oscar-export-field">
            <label for="download-port">Bridge port</label>
            <input id="download-port" class="o-input" type="number" min="1" max="65535" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="oscar-export-hint">
          Both are filled in with what this OSCAR reports for itself. Use the
          address other devices see, not <code>localhost</code>, unless the
          file will only ever be opened on this computer. If OSCAR moves later
          there is no need to download again: add
          <code>?oscar-host=ADDRESS&amp;oscar-port=PORT</code> to the page's
          address. A control whose Send when bridges data in does its bridging
          from this file, so open it in <strong>one copy</strong> only: every
          open copy sends.
        </p>
        <div id="download-error" class="oscar-export-error" style="display: none;"></div>
        <button id="download-button" class="o-btn o-btn-primary oscar-export-go" type="button">Download the file</button>
      </div>
    </div>  </div>
</div>

<!-- Running: every interface this OSCAR is serving in the background,
     whichever project is on the canvas. Opened from the RUNNING pill. -->
<div id="running-panel" style="display: none;">
  <div class="oscar-export">
    <p class="oscar-export-hint oscar-running-lead">
      OSCAR serves these in the background, whether or not their projects are
      open here. Click one to see its code.
    </p>
    <div class="oscar-publish-columns">
      <div id="published-box" class="oscar-published" style="display: none;">
        <ul id="published-list" class="oscar-published-list"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p id="running-empty" class="oscar-publish-off">Nothing is running. Publish a project and it appears here.</p>
  </div>
</div>
